# Kortex Context Integration
# This file is auto-populated by the .aim Neural VFS system

[INSTRUCTIONS]
This project uses Kortex (.aim) for zero-token context management.

When analyzing this codebase:
1. Check for .aim/memory.aim files in the project root or parent directories
2. The AIM proxy at http://127.0.0.1:1536 provides compressed context injection
3. Use the neuraldrive GUI to explore the 3D code graph for architecture understanding

## Project Structure
- `kortex/` - Main Rust workspace with AI-interactive memory system
  - `aim-proxy/` - Ollama MITM proxy (port 1536)
  - `neuraldrive/` - Tauri desktop app for 3D code visualization
  - `daemon/` - Memory management daemon
  - `vfs_layer/` - Virtual filesystem integration
  - `tui/` - Terminal UI

## Development Guidelines
- Always build with `cargo build --release` from kortex root
- The aim-proxy intercepts Ollama requests and injects compressed context
- NeuralDrive mounts projects and generates .aim memory tokens
- Token cost optimization: ~1 token per 50MB of project state via prefix caching

## Quick Start
1. Start Ollama: `ollama serve`
2. Start AIM-Proxy: `cd kortex && .\target\release\aim-proxy.exe`
3. Configure AI client to use http://127.0.0.1:1536
4. Launch NeuralDrive: `.\target\release\neuraldrive.exe`
